    <briefdescription>
<para>Heap-allocated node of an <computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_1_1_a_ring_tower" kindref="compound">ARingTower</ref></computeroutput> polynomial: a dense <computeroutput>degree</computeroutput>-indexed coefficient array that recurses through tower levels. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="struct_m2_1_1_a_ring_polynomial_struct_a552ba3616f5b4a33fa777ade2e344eaa_1a552ba3616f5b4a33fa777ade2e344eaa" kindref="member">deg</ref></computeroutput> is the polynomial&apos;s degree in the current top variable and <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_m2_1_1_a_ring_polynomial_struct_a8713184b110ed41dc09c92872f37275c_1a8713184b110ed41dc09c92872f37275c" kindref="member">len</ref></computeroutput> is the allocated capacity. The anonymous union picks the coefficient kind by depth: at the bottom level the coefficients are <computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_1_1_a_ring_z_zp_f_f_p_a_c_k_accaf1bd40bf4c6970206a8c1a4a71047_1accaf1bd40bf4c6970206a8c1a4a71047" kindref="member">ARingZZpFFPACK::ElementType</ref></computeroutput> values stored in <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_m2_1_1_a_ring_polynomial_struct_ad92345b7b933d2a73d1619ac95c1580b_1ad92345b7b933d2a73d1619ac95c1580b" kindref="member">coeffs</ref></computeroutput>, and at higher levels each &quot;coefficient&quot; is itself an <computeroutput><ref refid="group__polynomialrings_ga490857490c2a55400c60f9f0ff498f80_1ga490857490c2a55400c60f9f0ff498f80" kindref="member">ARingPolynomial</ref></computeroutput> one level down, stored in <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_m2_1_1_a_ring_polynomial_struct_aa917f1eab2223cdd8c8bd21fedd58db9_1aa917f1eab2223cdd8c8bd21fedd58db9" kindref="member">polys</ref></computeroutput>. Accessed through <computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_1_1_a_ring_tower" kindref="compound">ARingTower</ref></computeroutput> (the <computeroutput>aring</computeroutput>-shaped sibling of <computeroutput><ref refid="class_d_ring" kindref="compound">DRing</ref></computeroutput> in <computeroutput><ref refid="dpoly_8hpp" kindref="compound">dpoly.hpp</ref></computeroutput>), which always carries the current level so the right union arm is consulted. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
